"""Committed SPF v0.2 §8.5 negative-gap exponential ROM.

``q = 2^(-gap/256)`` for an integer log-code gap is evaluated as a shift plus a
256-entry fractional table (AlgRef v0.2 §8.5):

    k = gap >> 8          # integer part of gap/256
    f = gap & 255         # fractional index
    q = ldexp(ROM[f], -k)

The entries below are the IEEE-754 bit patterns of ``2^(-f/256)`` evaluated at
100 decimal digits with mpmath and rounded once to float64, so the table is
reproducible without depending on host ``libm``.  Scaling a normal float64 by a
power of two is exact, so the reconstruction is bit-identical to a
correctly-rounded ``exp2(-gap/256)`` over the whole ``uint16`` gap range —
:mod:`tests.v02.test_v02_exp2_neg_gap_rom` measures that on all 65536 gaps.

Generated by ``scripts/generate_spf_v02_exp2_rom.py``; the C mirror
``native/include/spf32_exp2_neg_gap_rom_v02.h`` is generated from this module by
``scripts/gen_exp2_neg_gap_rom_header.py``.
"""

